[[File:Wyrm icon.png|left]]
'''Lava Strykewyrms''' are [[Slayer monster]]s requiring 62 [[Slayer]] to kill, located in the [[Charred Dungeon]] beneath [[Charred Island]], requiring 60 [[Sailing]] to reach, as well as in the [[Wyrmscraig Cavern]] after partial completion of [[Fallen From Grace]]. They can be killed as part of a [[wyrm]] task, and are known for their [[dragon metal sheet]] drop, which is significantly more common when on a wyrm task.

Lava Strykewyrms attack with both [[melee]] and [[ranged]]. However, they use only melee when attacked from within one tile range of them, and only ranged when attacked from a distance. This means that all damage can be avoided with [[protection prayers]]. [[Fire spells]] will heal them equal to the amount hit. They are located in a single-way combat area and cannons cannot be used against them. Like wyrms, they are vulnerable to [[Dragonbane weapons|dragonbane]] weapons such as the [[dragon hunter lance]].

With the Slayer reward ''Bigger and Badder'' unlocked for 50 [[Slayer reward point]]s, there is a chance for their [[Superior slayer monster|superior]] version, the [[magma strykewyrm]], to spawn. The Slayer reward ''Can of Wyrms'' increases the number of wyrms assigned to 200-250 for the price of 100 Slayer reward points.

Just like regular wyrms, Lava Strykewyrms can be safespotted by out-ranging their attacks, but it requires a weapon with an [[attack range]] of 9 or 10.

